ned}x-y+z &=-8 \\\\ 2x-2y+3z &=-19.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672527 1072 #uuid "8805faad-2210-5845-9d51-28bb144681d1" 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672527 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3 & -19\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3 & -19\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=-5 \\\\ z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $y$. That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=y-5 \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=-3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}y-5 \\\\ y \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186672530 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672528 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672528 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z &=-7 \\\\ -x-y-z &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672528 1072 #uuid "906765ba-0e3a-569b-aee3-1e04419ce12f" 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672528 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=-1 \\\\ y+2z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and we have one free variable, $z$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=z-1 \\\\ y &=-2z-3 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}z-1 \\\\ -2z-3 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672529 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}y-5 \\\\ y \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672529 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538693 17592186045443 true] [17592186672529 1083